{:edb/db-before-t 549 :edb/db-after-t 550 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533862 50 #inst "2026-10-05T04:54:51.780Z" 13194139533862 true] [17592186068789 1020 #edb/ref 17592186256328 13194139533862 true] [17592186068789 1020 #edb/ref 17592186256335 13194139533862 true] [17592186068945 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533862 true] [17592186068945 1145 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+10t+13 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}+10t & =-13 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot t & =-13 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot t+{5}^{2}-{5}^{2} & =-13 \\\\ (t+5)^{2}-25 & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t+5)^{2}-25 & =-13 \\\\ (t+5)^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=5,$ $q=12,$ and $p+q=17.$" 13194139533862 true] [17592186069140 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533862 true] [17592186069140 1145 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+4 & =9 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2} & =5 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2})-4 & =5 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-4 & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}-4 & =5 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=-2,q=9,$ and $p+q=7.$\n\nNow, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-2)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2+3=5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2-3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=5.$ Thus, the sum is $4.$" 13194139533862 true] [17592186069189 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533862 true] [17592186069189 1145 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+8x-33 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x & =33 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =33 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot x+{4}^{2})-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16 & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square and solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}-16 & =33 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=49,$ and $p+q=53.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =49 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe simplify the two solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4+7=3 \\\\ x & =-4-7=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-11$ and $x=3.$" 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1017 #edb/ref 17592186256329 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1089 "q-112487" 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1100 "The equation ${m}^{2}+8=-8m$ can be written in the form $(m+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1113 #uuid "6d70e8a4-cad6-5c6f-b225-88fe32f8d423" 13194139533862 true] [17592186256328 1145 "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, the $-8m$ term to the left-hand side, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+8 & =-8m \\\\ {m}^{2}+8m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m & =-8 \\\\ {m}^{2}+2\\cdot 4\\cdot m+{4}^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2}-{4}^{2} & =-8 \\\\ (m+4)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $p=4,q=8,$ and $p+q=12.$\n\nNext, we solve the equation using the square-root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+4)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\sqrt{(m+4)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ |m+4| & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ m+4 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ m & =-4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{ali